 extract($a) { return 7; } echo extract([1]);\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")))\\\\\\\\n       (is (= \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"9\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (out \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"<?php namespace N; function compact($a) { return 9; } echo compact('x');\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))))))\\\\\\\\ncommit 004dfb4444ecf026acf70e7d64e45b4041d5ed72\\\\\\\\nAuthor: Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\\\\\\\\nDate:   Fri Nov 6 02:01:48 2026 +0700\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    fix(yang.php): the ruled empty-buffer notice — php/warn errno 8 + false\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc\\\\\\\\nindex 8c6e7619..39b6b622 100644\\\\\\\\n--- a/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc\\\\\\\\n+++ b/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc\\\\\\\\n@@ -391,16 +391,22 @@\\\\\\\\n      (fn [args]\\\\\\\\n        (let [bufs (cell/get php.rt/out)]\\\\\\\\n          (if (= (data/count bufs) 1)\\\\\\\\n-           false\\\\\\\\n+           (do (php/warn 8 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ob_end_clean(): Failed to delete buffer. No buffer to delete\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") false)\\\\\\\\n            (do (cell/set! php.rt/out (php/args-prefix bufs (- (data/count bufs) 1) 0 [])) true))))]\\\\\\\\n     [php/bi-ob-get-clean\\\\\\\\n      (fn [args]\\\\\\\\n-       (let [s (php/bi-ob-get-contents args)]\\\\\\\\n-         (if (= s false) false (do (php/bi-ob-end-clean args) s))))]\\\\\\\\n+       (let [bufs (cell/get php.rt/out)]\\\\\\\\n+         (if (= (data/count bufs) 1)\\\\\\\\n+           (do (php/warn 8 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ob_get_clean(): Failed to delete buffer. No buffer to delete\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") false)\\\\\\\\n+           (let [s (php/bi-ob-get-contents args)]\\\\\\\\n+             (do (php/bi-ob-end-clean args) s)))))]\\\\\\\\n     [php/bi-ob-end-flush\\\\\\\\n      (fn [args]\\\\\\\\n-       (let [s (php/bi-ob-get-contents args)]\\\\\\\\n-         (if (= s false) false (do (php/bi-ob-end-clean args) (php/echo s) true))))]\\\\\\\\n+       (let [bufs (cell/get php.rt/out)]\\\\\\\\n+         (if (= (data/count bufs) 1)\\\\\\\\n+           (do (php/warn 8 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ob_end_flush(): Failed to delete and flush buffer. No buffer to delete or flush\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") false)\\\\\\\\n+           (let [s (php/bi-ob-get-contents args)]\\\\\\\\n+             (do (php/bi-ob-end-clean args) (php/echo s) true)))))]\\\\\\\\n     [php/headers-refused?\\\\\\\\n      (fn []\\\\\\\\n        (if (cell/get php.rt/headers-sent)\\\\\\\\ndiff --git a/test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p5.cljc b/test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p5.cljc\\\\\\\\nindex 04c03b27..f5dbdb29 100644\\\\\\\\n--- a/test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p5.cljc\\\\\\\\n+++ b/test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p5.cljc\\\\\\\\n@@ -39,7 +39,8 @@\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"aabc\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n    (fx :output-buffer-flush\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"<?php ob_start(); echo 'a'; ob_end_flush(); echo 'b'; var_dump(ob_end_clean());\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n-       \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"abbool(false)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n+       \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"abbool(false)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n+       :diag [[8 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ob_end_clean(): Failed to delete buffer. No buffer to delete\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]])\\\\\\\\n    (fx :headers-cookies-status\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"<?php header('X-One: 1'); setcookie('sid', 'abc'); http_response_code(201); echo http_response_code();\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"201\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n# Findings — Round B1-r2 residuals (engineer)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nBranch: `feat/roundB1-p9-contracts`. All six architect residuals fixed in\\\\\\\\nthe prelude sources, each with a regression in\\\\\\\\n`test/yang/php/antlr/builtin_surfaces_test.clj`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 1. P1 — json_encode nested failure (fixed)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRoot cause: `php/json-encode` concatenated `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`/`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"` onto the result of\\\\\\\\n`php/json-array-values`/`php/json-array-pairs` unconditionally. A failed\\\\\\\\nchild (e.g. `INF`) answers `false`, and the host string primitive refuses\\\\\\\\na delimiter + `false` — the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"data primitive refused\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" host error at the old\\\\\\\\nline 648. Fix: new `php/json-encode-value` gate passes the child through\\\\\\\\nwhen it is not a string (throw mode already threw inside the child; quiet\\\\\\\\nmode already warned once there, so no double warning). `json_encode([INF])`\\\\\\\\nnow warns `[2 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Inf and NaN cannot be JSON encoded\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]` and answers `false`;\\\\\\\\nwith `JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR` it throws `JsonException`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 2. P2 — strrpos negative offsets (fixed)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNegative offsets now start that many characters from the end and search\\\\\\\\nback from there (`hi = len + off`, clamped to `len - nn`), instead of\\\\\\\\nshrinking the upper bound by the needle length. `strrpos(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"hello\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"l\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",-2)`\\\\\\\\nis 3. `off > len` or `off < -len` throws `ValueError` (\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"must be contained\\\\\\\\nin argument #1 ($haystack)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), and an empty needle is a `ValueError`.\\\\\\\\n`test/builtin_surfaces_test.clj:37` corrected 2 → 3 plus two ValueError pins.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 3. P2 — diff/intersect string comparison + unique dispatch (fixed)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n`php/p9-diff-others` used loose `php/p9-search`, so `array_diff([\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1.0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"],[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"])`\\\\\\\\nwas empty. New `php/p9-diff-str-has?` compares `php/p9-string` forms:\\\\\\\\nthe diff keeps `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1.0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`. `php/p9-unique-eq?` dispatch was off by one\\\\\\\\n(1 = loose, 2 = numeric); now 0 = `SORT_REGULAR` loose, 1 = `SORT_NUMERIC`,\\\\\\\\nelse string — so default `array_unique(['1.0','1'])` keeps one value and\\\\\\\\n`SORT_STRING` keeps both.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 4. P2 — array_splice replacement conversion (fixed)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nReplacements now pass through `php/p9-splice-repl`, which re-indexes values\\\\\\\\n(discarding string keys); an explicit `null` replacement is the empty array\\\\\\\\ninstead of a one-element `[null]`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 5. P2 — JSON grammar/depth/options (fixed)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- `php/json-number-end` no longer accepts `+`, so `json_decode(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"+1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")` fails.\\\\\\\\n- `php/json-read-string-loop` rejects raw control bytes (< 32).\\\\\\\\n- Decode depth counter starts at 1, so `[1]` at depth 1 fails\\\\\\\\n  (\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Maximum stack depth exceeded\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\").\\\\\\\\n- `json_encode` takes its depth argument (default 512, `< 1` is a\\\\\\\\n  `ValueError`) and enforces it instead of a hardcoded 512.\\\\\\\\n- Flags outside the supported masks are refused with an `Error` naming the\\\\\\\\n  function (encode: only `JSON_PRETTY_PRINT` + `JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR`;\\\\\\\\n  decode: only `JSON_OBJECT_AS_ARRAY` + `JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR`).\\\\\\\\n  `JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR` propagation itself was already wired through\\\\\\\\n  `php/json-fail` / `php/json-encode-fail`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 6. P2 — extract/compact residuals (fixed)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- `EXTR_PREFIX_ONLY_IF_EXISTS` (= 7) is present in `builtins.cljc`.\\\\\\\\n- `php/extract-name` always keeps the `_` separator, so an empty prefix\\\\\\\\n  imports `$_z`, and `EXTR_PREFIX_ALL` imports numeric keys (`$p_0`).\\\\\\\\n- `php/bi-extract` validates: mode outside 0–7 is a `ValueError`; a prefix\\\\\\\\n  mode without a third argument, or with a non-variable-name prefix, is a\\\\\\\\n  `ValueError` (empty prefix stays legal per the underscore rule; `EXTR_REFS`\\\\\\\\n  keeps its existing `Error`).\\\\\\\\n- `compact(1)` warns `[2 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"compact(): Each argument must be a string or an\\\\\\\\n  array of strings\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]` and skips instead of silently dropping.\\\\\\\\n- Fixture `:extract-skip-and-prefix` in `programs_p9.cljc` pinned the old\\\\\\\\n  naming (`$p_z` + diag); updated to `$p__z` with out `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"156\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\