parison, JSON encoding still warns and permits the cited depth overflow, and the nonexistent extraction constant remains. I’m checking the measurement provenance and source references before the final verdict.\\\\nFocused probes on `06cd429f` reproduced those B1 residuals. The grammar change also rejects valid `1e+2`. The negative-offset `strrpos` probe and empty-buffer diagnostic pass. I independently validated the manifest’s 95 unique quick IDs and six slow records, but haven’t located retained tree/run references for the older `bug44069` and `bug40809` measurements.\\\\nReviewed `origin/feat/p8-legacy-retirement` at **`06cd429fed006a406a8cdd354c54dbc7484a650a`**.\\\\n\\\\n**(a) DEFECT — provenance remains unconfirmed.** The manifest parses: **95 unique quick IDs, six slow records**, both passing records removed, and timeout/resource classes distinguished correctly. However, the inspected artifacts still lack measured-tree hashes and run references for the older `bug44069` and `bug40809` measurements. Your brief identifies the final-tip `bug63055` verification; my local repeat reached its review cutoff without a result.\\\\n\\\\n**(b) CONFIRMED.** The no-buffer arms emit errno **8**, preserve the recorded messages, and return **false**. The fixture compares diagnostics directly, without suppression. A focused `ob_end_clean()` probe reproduced the exact notice and `false`.\\\\n\\\\n**(c) DEFECT.** B1-r2 removes the nested-encoding host error and repairs several counterexamples, but focused probes on this tip reproduce remaining defects:\\\\n\\\\n- **Array comparison:** default `array_unique([\\\\\\\"1.0\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\"])` retains one value; PHP requires two because its default is `SORT_STRING`. The test now pins the wrong default. [Implementation](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:526), [PHP source](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/php-8.3.35/ext/standard/array.c).\\\\n- **JSON failure/depth:** `json_e