cords** check out. Residuals:\\n   - `bug40809` still carries `:feature :undefined-builtin` despite its timeout result.\\n   - This tree already registers `str_replace`, defines `php/bi-str-replace`, and includes those definitions in the prelude. The retained undefined-function observation needs reconciliation with that tree.\\n   - The fold supplies no measured-tree hash or run-evidence reference establishing the claimed measurements. Retain those before confirmation; no replacement outcome should be inferred statically.\\n\\nRead-only review; no files changed or behavioral suites rerun. Only the exact P1 commit has renewed landing authority.\\nLOG 1794720000000-architect-confirm-round.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\\nI’ll check the architecture rules and both commits, then give each unit a verdict. For P8, I’ll distinguish approval of the procedure from confirmation of the pending measured records.\\nI’m using the code-review-pr skill for this confirmation pass, focused on the cited fixes and their acceptance boundaries.\\nThe P1 diff removes the out-of-scope `fesc` reference and places the drain after the shutdown escape. The P8 manifest still has the three stale records, consistent with the remeasurement being pending. I’m checking the P9 edge cases and P1 fatal-bypass path before assigning verdicts.\\nP9 still has contract defects despite the reported green gate: diff/intersect use loose equality, negative `strrpos` offsets remain wrong, and JSON encoding does not propagate nested failure correctly. The new tests also assert a nonexistent extraction constant. I’m checking the counterexamples against PHP 8.3 source so the required follow-up is concrete.\\nFocused JVM probes reproduced the P9 failures: nested `json_encode([INF])` raises a host error, `json_decode(\\\"+1\\\")` returns `1`, and encoding ignores the supplied depth. For P1, the bundled closure check and linked-module manifest construction pass, and the shutdown-exit case returns `\\\"AS\\\"` with status `3`.\\n**1. `d5f120d0` — CONFIRMED.**\\n\\nThe follow-up resolves both findings, including the linked-module boundary.\\n\\n- Bundled free-name checking returns no stray names; `module-spec` constructs successfully.\\n- The shutdown-exit probe returns **`\\\"AS\\\"`, status `3`**.\\n- Injecting `php/root-fatal` during the buffered shutdown callback returns **empty output and fatal `\\\"boom\\\"`**, bypassing the drain.\\n\\nThe seat may land this unit. [Corrected fallback and drain placement](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5189).\\n\\n**2. `0aa234e9` — DEFECT. Hold landing.**\\n\\nEmpty-search handling, nontruncating padding, single-array mapping keys, variadic mapping, null-binding existence, missing-name compact warnings, and the declaration-based resolution guard are repaired. Residual defects remain:\\n\\n- **P1 — Nested JSON encoding failure escapes into a host error.** `json_encode([INF])` reproduces `\\\"data primitive refused\\\"`: the array encoder concatenates its opening delimiter with the child’s `false` result. Without throw mode, PHP returns `false` without the newly introduced warning. [Encoder](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:648), [PHP 8.3 implementation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/json/json.c).\\n\\n- **P2 — Negative `strrpos` offsets remain incorrect.** `strrpos(\\\"hello\\\", \\\"l\\\", -2)` reproduces **2**; PHP requires **3**. The new test pins the wrong answer. Offsets outside the haystack also need `ValueError`. [Implementation](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:52), [incorrect assertion](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/test/yang/php/antlr/builtin_surfaces_test.clj:37), [PHP source](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/standard/string.c).\\n\\n- **P2 — Array comparisons remain wrong.** Diff/intersect still use loose equality: `count(array_diff([\\\"1.0\\\"], [\\\"1\\\"]))` reproduces **0**, requiring **1** under [PHP’s string comparison](https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.array-diff.php). Unique’s flag dispatch is also misnumbered: `SORT_REGULAR` is **0**, numeric **1**, string **2**. The regular-mode counterexample reproduces two retained values instead of one. [Comparison code](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:503), [PHP flag definitions](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/standard/php_array.h).\\n\\n- **P2 — Splice replacement conversion is incomplete.** Reusing `spread-loop` preserves replacement string keys, which PHP discards. Explicit `null` becomes one null element instead of an empty replacement array. [Splice implementation](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:431), [PHP contract](https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.array-splice.php).\\n\\n- **P2 — JSON grammar, depth, and options remain incomplete.** `json_decode(\\\"+1\\\")` reproduces integer **1**; raw control characters are also accepted. Encoding ignores argument 3: `json_encode([[1]], 0, 1)` succeeds. Decoding depth starts one level too low: `[1]` at depth 1 succeeds instead of failing. Other unsupported flags remain silently accepted. [Number parser](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:761), [depth/options](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:695), [PHP scanner](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/json/json_scanner.re), [PHP depth initialization](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/json/json_parser.y).\\n\\n- **P2 — Extract/compact completion is overstated.** `EXTR_PREFIX_ONLY_IF_EXISTS` remains a nonexistent constant, now asserted by the tests. Invalid extraction modes, missing required prefixes, and invalid prefixes lack required validation. `EXTR_PREFIX_ALL` incorrectly rejects numeric keys: the focused probe imports **0** variables for `[0 => 5]` with prefix `\\\"p\\\"`; PHP imports `$p_0`. Empty prefixes also lose the mandatory underscore. `compact(1)` silently skips its required warning. [Constants](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/builtins.cljc:169), [extract/compact](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_module.cljc:200), [PHP extraction and compact implementation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/standard/array.c).\\n\\nThe reported **3/135/0** gate therefore does not establish contract completion. Correct the erroneous assertions and cover these counterexamples.\\n\\n**3. P8 manifest — CONFIRMED-WITH-EDITS, pending measured fold.**\\n\\n**The remeasure-and-fold procedure satisfies my ruling.** No additional semantic requirement is imposed.\\n\\nFor `bug44069`, `bug40809`, and `bug63055`:\\n\\n- Remove records that now pass.\\n- For remaining failures, fold the measured result and update the classification/work item.\\n- Retain the measured tree identity and run evidence; distinguish resource failures or timeouts from guest results.\\n\\nI independently checked **95 unique quick IDs**, matching descriptions and recorded total. The three stale slow records remain in the inspected artifact. The seat may land after folding the measurements and checking manifest consistency; this is conditional authority, not confirmation of results still pending.\\n\\nRead-only review completed with focused JVM probes and static/source checks. No files changed or suites rerun.\\nLOG 1794820000000-architect-confirm3.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\\nI’ll use the code-review-pr skill to check the origin tips, follow-up diffs, and recorded evidence, then issue a landing verdict for each branch.\\nThe requested commits are available locally, but the local origin refs for P1 and P5 are older, and the remote lookup failed. I’ll verify the remote tips separately and check the exact commits meanwhile. P8 also has a later fold commit, `dbe9e072`, containing the timeout record described in your brief.\\nThe live remote tips differ from the brief: P1 is at `0eade311` and P5 at `e39e1912`; neither includes its follow-up commit. P8 is at `dbe9e072`. I also found a P5 residual: the test drops the empty-buffer notice, but the recorded Verdict 2 explicitly required the engine to emit it and prohibited normalizing it away.\\nP8’s manifest parses and has 95 unique quick IDs and 7 slow records. Two residuals prevent confirmation: `bug40809` still has `:feature :undefined-builtin`, and the claim that `str_replace` is absent conflicts with the reviewed tree, which registers and includes its implementation. The fold lacks a measured-tree hash and run-evidence reference to reconcile that conflict.\\n1. **P1 — CONFIRMED for `d5f120d0`; origin-tip DEFECT.** The commit matches the previously confirmed escape/drain repair. **The seat may land `d5f120d0`.** However, live origin still points to `0eade311`, which lacks that repair. Advance origin before merging.\\n\\n2. **P5 — DEFECT.** Fixture repair, class-derived errno comparison, ordered request vectors, exit-status checking, and P5 banner are confirmed in `a7cf7a0f`. But `request_context_test.clj:36` removes the empty-`ob_end_clean` notice. Verdict 2 explicitly required emitting errno **8** in the engine and prohibited normalizing away this missing diagnostic. The reported **3/35/0** therefore does not close that finding. Also, live origin remains at `e39e1912`, without `a7cf7a0f`.\\n\\n3. **P8 — DEFECT at actual origin tip `dbe9e072`** (`514fae8d` plus timeout fold). Manifest parsing and **95 unique quick IDs / 7 slow records** check out. Residuals:\\n   - `bug40809` still carries `:feature :undefined-builtin` despite its timeout result.\\n   - This tree already registers `str_replace`, defines `php/bi-str-replace`, and includes those definitions in the prelude. The retained undefined-function observation needs reconciliation with that tree.\\n   - The fold supplies no measured-tree hash or run-evidence reference establishing the claimed measurements. Retain those before confirmation; no replacement outcome should be inferred statically.\\n\\nRead-only review; no files changed or behavioral suites rerun. Only the exact P1 commit has renewed landing authority.\\n\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/orch-lane/1795060000000-architect-p8-final-confirm3.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:53:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_26\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"/Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/babashka/1.13.225/bb -e '(require (quote [clojure.edn :as edn])) (let [m (edn/read-string (slurp \\\\\\\"test/yang/php/antlr/phpt_quick_mismatch_manifest.edn\\\\\\\"))] (prn {:slow-records (count (:slow-known-gaps m)) :provenance (mapv (juxt :id :measured-at) (:slow-known-gaps m)) :quick-ids (count (set (mapcat :entries (:known-gaps m))))}))'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"{:slow-records 6, :provenance [[\\\"Zend/tests/gc_013.phpt\\\" {:tree \\\"unrecorded\\\", :host \\\"shiva\\\", :date \\\"2026-11-04\\\", :log \\\"~/ci/rm-phpt-quick.log\\\"}] [\\\"Zend/tests/gc_023.phpt\\\" {:tree \\\"unrecorded\\\", :host \\\"shiva\\\", :date \\\"2026-11-04\\\", :log \\\"~/ci/rm-phpt-quick.log\\\"}] [\\\"Zend/tests/bug39438.phpt\\\" {:tree \\\"unrecorded\\\", :host \\\"shiva\\\", :date \\\"2026-11-04\\\", :log \\\"~/ci/rm-phpt-quick.log\\\"}] [\\\"Zend/tests/bug64660.phpt\\\" {:tree \\\"unrecorded\\\", :host \\\"shiva\\\", :date \\\"2026-11-04\\\", :log \\\"~/ci/rm-phpt-quick.log\\\"}] [\\\"Zend/tests/bug40809.phpt\\\" {:tree \\\"dbe9e072\\\", :host \\\"shiva\\\", :date \\\"2026-11-05\\\", :log \\\"~/ci/rm-40809-long.log\\\"}] [\\\"Zend/tests/gc_012.phpt\\\" {:tree \\\"unrecorded\\\", :host \\\"shiva\\\", :date \\\"2026-11-04\\\", :log \\\"~/ci/rm-phpt-quick.log\\\"}]], :quick-ids 95}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/orch-lane/1795060000000-architect-p8-final-confirm3.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:54:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_27\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"**CONFIRMED — landing authority for `359c0378c221189e930dcf86462451b92f6768da`.**\\n\\n1. Provenance: five earlier records honestly mark trees `unrecorded`; `bug40809` cites `dbe9e072`, November 5, within the specified November 4/5 window. Passing records remain removed.\\n2. Depth: `[1]` at depth 1 succeeds; `[[1]]` fails. Regression corrected.\\n3. Scanner: `.1` and `1.` rejected; `1e+2` accepted.\\n\\nIndependent focused JVM check: **1 test, 76 assertions, 0 failures/errors**. Manifest: **95 unique quick IDs, six slow records**. Read-only; no files changed.\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
