{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/collab/orch-lane/1795070000000-engineer-roundB2-r2.muse-spark-1.3-contributor.findings.md; nl -ba src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj | sed -n '95,165p;420,495p;520,548p'; ls /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/target*; rg -n 'b2|lifecycle|shiva' collab/orch-lane/1795250000000*\"","aggregated_output":"Created-Local: 2026-11-07 +0700\nCoding-Agent: muse (muse-spark-1.3-contributor, laptop)\nWorktree: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2 (branch feat/p5b2-lifecycle)\n\n# Task: Round B2-r2 — the step-7 fix list (items 1-10)\n\nThe architect step-7 findings file named in the task\n(collab/orch-lane/1795050000001-architect-b2-escalations-step7.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md)\nis absent from this checkout, so the rulings below are implemented from the\nitem text in /tmp/muse-b2r2.md plus the step-7 retro review\n(collab/orch-lane/1794580000001-reviewer-retro-step7.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md,\nsection 2). PHP 8.3 behavior (trigger_error ValueError message) confirmed by\nweb search against php-src-derived reports.\n\n## Per-item changes\n\n### 1. Init-time raise (prelude.cljc run-main, php/raise)\n- Request binding moved inside the root protected region: run-main installs\n  the fatal/exit escapes first, then binds the request inside the body\n  `php/try`, before the body. An init-time throw-error is now delivered to\n  that handler and ends as the ordinary `:php/uncaught` snapshot rendered\n  \"PHP Fatal error: Uncaught ...\"; never an array key or Error-valued data.\n- The empty-stack branch of `php/raise` is now `php/invariant-violation`, a\n  defect-loud host-level failure (a deliberately arity-wrong `cell/new`\n  through `php/missing-invariant-trap`); it does NOT call `php/root-fatal`\n  (which would recurse through `php/raise` with no escape installed).\n\n### 2. Invalid trigger_error levels are ValueError (prelude.cljc, programs_p5b2)\n- `bi-trigger-error` throws catchable\n  `ValueError(\"trigger_error(): Argument #2 ($error_level) must be one of\n  E_USER_ERROR, E_USER_WARNING, E_USER_NOTICE, or E_USER_DEPRECATED\")`\n  for anything outside 256/512/1024/16384 (PHP 8.3); uncaught it is the\n  ordinary snapshot. No `E_WARNING`/false.\n- Fixture `:trigger-invalid-level-rejected` replaced by\n  `:trigger-invalid-level-throws-value-error` (uncaught ValueError) plus a\n  caught case `:trigger-invalid-level-caught`.\n\n### 3. :linked accepts requests (lower.cljc, linked_harness, test)\n- `lower/lower-program` already emits the request as `run-main`'s second\n  operand for BOTH profiles; verified the `:linked` path shares the same\n  `main` node and `option-keys` keeps `:request`.\n- `linked-harness/run-fixture` passes `:request` through to lowering, so the\n  importing task instantiates request state; new\n  `linked-profile-consumes-request-and-isolates-test` covers linked request\n  consumption, sequential-run isolation, and asserts no live request cell\n  (`rt/request`, `rt/response`, `rt/out`, `rt/diag`) is a module export\n  (core/exports only keeps the `php` namespace; `php.rt/*` stays qualified).\n\n### 4. Integer-key request merge (prelude.cljc, programs_p5b2)\n- `php/request-merge-keys` preserves integer keys for BOTH kinds: colliding\n  scalars overwrite in order, both-arrays recurse (`php/request-merge-into`),\n  new keys put. The numeric fixture now expects `3020post`\n  (GET ids[0]=10/ids[1]=20, POST ids[0]=30 overwrites; no ids[2] — the old\n  `102030post` append expectation was wrong).\n- New fixtures: sparse integer keys (`:request-merge-sparse-integers`) and\n  integer-key nested collisions (`:request-merge-nested-integer-collision`).\n\n### 5. E_USER_ERROR default fatal (prelude.cljc, programs_p5b2)\n- Handled (matching handler returning non-false) continues; absent/excluded/\n  false-returning takes the explicit default fatal path.\n- The default fatal is a distinct guest-fatal reason (`php/guest-fatal`,\n  terminal `:guest-fatal`), NOT the operational termination: it escapes the\n  body past handlers/finally, while run-main still runs shutdown functions,\n  drains buffers and marks objects destructed on the way out, then answers\n  `:php/fatal`. Shutdown-phase guest-fatals route through the shutdown\n  escape the same way.\n- Tests: shutdown output, buffered output, handled continuation,\n  false-returning fallback.\n\n### 6. Stream lifecycle (closed at the composition level)\n- New `portable-harness/run-lifecycle-raw` (shared JVM/Node/Dart lane):\n  the request record is appended to a composition-supplied request stream\n  (the composition's own ring-buffer constructor) and consumed back from it\n  via oldest-cursor/next; the consumed record rides the production channel\n  as `run-main`'s second operand; every response and diagnostic record is\n  emitted on composition-supplied response/diagnostics streams and drained\n  back. Returns the drained `{:response [...] :diag [...]}` alongside the\n  task value.\n- `lower-through-stage` / `run-packet-raw` accept an optional request, so\n  the portable lane can carry requests at all (previously request-less).\n- New `stream-lifecycle-consumes-and-emits-over-streams-test`: superglobal\n  seeding from the consumed record, diagnostic emission (`E_USER_NOTICE`\n  `boom`), header-then-body emission order, nil-request defaults, drained\n  streams equal to the task value's `:php/response`/`:php/diag`, and\n  cross-harness `run-raw` output agreement.\n- Record transport over the link (`:link-request`/`:link-response`) streams\n  is NOT re-architected: the guest still answers its value map and the host\n  emits the records. Guest-level stream effects would need engine support\n  (prelude sexps cannot express `:stream/put` nodes).\n\n### 7. http_response_code(0), status lines, header replacement\n- `http_response_code(0)` is a getter (answers current, installs nothing).\n- The claimed status-line parsing is implemented: an `HTTP/...` line sets\n  the response code from its first status token.\n- Repeated same-name headers replace case-insensitively on the field name\n  (new `php/emit-header!`); `replace=false` still appends.\n- Tests for zero-getter, status-line code, and case-insensitive replacement.\n\n### 8. setcookie (prelude.cljc, programs_p5b2)\n- Max SEVEN positional args; the array form rejects extra positionals\n  (both ValueError). Option names match case-insensitively; unknown or\n  numeric keys throw\n  `ValueError(\"setcookie(): Unknown option '...'\")`. SameSite supported in\n  the options array.\n- Note: options-array values are now retained as given (no per-slot\n  coercion); existing fixture record shapes unchanged.\n\n### 9. Handler mask fixture\n- Now two distinct handlers with two distinct masks, restoring the earlier\n  pair: B(E_USER_NOTICE) stacked over A(E_USER_WARNING); w1 sinks, n1 hits\n  B, restore brings back A (w2 hits A), second restore returns to default\n  (w3 sinks). Out `B1024A512`, diag `[[512 w1] [512 w3]]`.\n\n### 10. Oracle runner (oracle.clj)\n- Enumerates B2: `run-p5b2` / `check-p5b2-fixture` / `--p5b2`;\n  `--print-prologue` also resolves B2 ids (docker-free dry run).\n- The request serializer accepts nested values (recursive\n  `php-value-literal`); the prologue uses the ruled recursive merge\n  (`yang_request_merge`, POST wins per key, nested arrays merge) instead of\n  `array_merge`.\n- The fatal parser preserves the new guest-fatal representation (`:fatal`,\n  distinct from `:uncaught`); B2 checks compare engine `:fatal` against it.\n- Initial-status treatment: bare CLI starts WITHOUT the assumed HTTP 200 —\n  status fixtures declare `:http-profile` and the B2 prologue installs the\n  explicit initial 200 scaffold for them.\n\n## Verification (laptop)\n\n- `clojure -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.p5b2-lifecycle-test\n  -n yang.php.antlr.request-context-test -n yang.php.antlr.prelude-test\n  -n yang.php.antlr.class-model-test`: 47 tests / 1095 assertions,\n  0 failures, 0 errors.\n- `clj -M:kondo --lint` on the four touched files: 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- `cljstyle check` on the four touched files: clean (after one `fix` pass).\n- Oracle dry run (no docker):\n  `clojure -M:oracle -m yang.php.oracle --print-prologue\n  request-merge-nested-integer-collision` renders the nested serializer +\n  ruled recursive merge; `status-answers-previous` appends the explicit\n  `http_response_code(200);` HTTP-profile scaffold.\n- NOT run locally per gate: e2e / slow / subsystem (seat gates on shiva).\n\n## Open questions / seat follow-ups\n\n- The `cell/new`-arity trap for `php/raise`'s empty stack is loud but\n  indirect; a dedicated host-level invariant primitive would be cleaner.\n- Item 6 is closed at the composition level; link-stream transport stays out.\n- All new/changed B2 fixtures stay `:oracle :pending` for the shiva\n  `php:8.3` pass, especially: ValueError texts, guest-fatal pairing,\n  SameSite/unknown-option texts, merge order, header emission order.\n    95\t(defn- strip-location\n    96\t  ([s file] (strip-location s file nil))\n    97\t  ([s file unit-dir]\n    98\t   (str/replace s\n    99\t                (re-pattern (str \" in /w/\" (location-pattern file unit-dir) \" on line \\\\d+\"))\n   100\t                \"\")))\n   101\t\n   102\t\n   103\t(defn parse-stdout\n   104\t  \"Parse PHP CLI stdout for `/w/<file>` into\n   105\t   `{:out <string> :diag [[errno msg] ...] :uncaught {:class c :message m}-or-nil}`.\n   106\t   With `unit-dir`, locations in any file below `/w/<unit-dir>` are stripped\n   107\t   (a multi-unit fixture).\"\n   108\t  ([raw file] (parse-stdout raw file nil))\n   109\t  ([raw file unit-dir]\n   110\t   (let [qfile (location-pattern file unit-dir)\n   111\t         strip-location (fn [s file] (strip-location s file unit-dir))\n   112\t         ;; The uncaught block ends at PHP's own terminator, so output written\n   113\t         ;; after it (shutdown functions, destructors) s