er_error('boom', E_USER_ERROR); echo 'C';\\\\\\\"\\\\n+       base-request \\\\\\\"A\\\\\\\"\\\\n+       :diag [[256 \\\\\\\"boom\\\\\\\"]] :oracle :pending\\\\n+       :fatal \\\\\\\"boom\\\\\\\")\\\\n+   (fx :trigger-invalid-level-rejected\\\\n+       \\\\\\\"<?php var_dump(trigger_error('x', 9999));\\\\\\\"\\\\n+       base-request \\\\\\\"bool(false)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\\n+       :diag [[2 \\\\\\\"trigger_error(): Invalid error level\\\\\\\"]] :oracle :pending\\\\n+       :response [{:php.response/body \\\\\\\"bool(false)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"}])\\\\n+   (fx :handler-mask-saved-and-restored\\\\n+       (str \\\\\\\"<?php set_error_handler(function($n, $s) { echo 'H', $n; return true; }, E_USER_WARNING);\\\\\\\"\\\\n+            \\\\\\\" trigger_error('w1', E_USER_WARNING);\\\\\\\"\\\\n+            \\\\\\\" trigger_error('n1', E_USER_NOTICE);\\\\\\\"\\\\n+            \\\\\\\" restore_error_handler();\\\\\\\"\\\\n+            \\\\\\\" trigger_error('w2', E_USER_WARNING);\\\\\\\")\\\\n+       base-request \\\\\\\"H512\\\\\\\"\\\\n+       :diag [[1024 \\\\\\\"n1\\\\\\\"] [512 \\\\\\\"w2\\\\\\\"]] :oracle :pending\\\\n+       :response [{:php.response/body \\\\\\\"H512\\\\\\\"}])])\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ncollab/orch-lane/1795050000000-architect-b2-escalations-step7.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:24:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_11\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"rg -n '\\\\\\\"'^##|''^###|request|publication|8'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.10|8\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.11|linked' docs/design/yang.php.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"9:progress through the linked inclusion profile, dynamic scope, namespaces,\\\\n41:  php-src selection, the full permutation corpus and the linked profile (P4\\\\n51:its section 8.11 for PHP arrays, and Phase 3. Companion:\\\\n62:## 1. Scope\\\\n66:mixed HTML text, to the Universal AST, and runs one request as one task\\\\n67:reading an explicit request record. The frontend id is `:yang/php` either\\\\n82:3. superglobals are built from an explicit request input;\\\\n84:5. two requests share nothing.\\\\n88:## 2. Prerequisites\\\\n92:parsing with three-host execution, the linked-profile matrix of bundled on\\\\n93:four evaluators and linked on three until L-b), and the ADR 0004 dependency.\\\\n98:publication-time-unavailable imports (section 11.3).\\\\n100:## 3. The paradigm specification\\\\n102:### 3.1 Reference runtime\\\\n111:### 3.2 Arrays and keys\\\\n137:#### 3.2.1 Reads, `isset`, `empty`, `unset` and builtins (P2)\\\\n179:### 3.3 Scope\\\\n202:  insertion-ordered, with the superglobals pre-seeded from the request record.\\\\n206:### 3.4 Superglobals and the request context\\\\n208:- A PHP run is one task consuming one **request record** from a\\\\n209:  composition-supplied stream: `{:php.request/method :uri :query :headers\\\\n212:  pinned `request_order`) and, for CLI, `$argv` and `$argc`. `$_SESSION` is a\\\\n223:- Cross-request leakage is impossible by construction: one task per request\\\\n226:### 3.5 Coercion, comparison and arithmetic\\\\n259:### 3.6 Null\\\\n264:### 3.7 Classes, interfaces, traits and enums\\\\n308:### 3.8 Functions and the tables\\\\n319:### 3.9 Exceptions, warnings and `@`\\\\n341:### 3.10 Generators and iteration protocols\\\\n350:### 3.11 Mixed HTML mode\\\\n358:### 3.12 eval\\\\n360:`eval` is a new compilation request (`yang.antlr.md` 8.6) sharing the caller's\\\\n364:## 4. The reference, array and object lifecycle\\\\n373:### 4.1 What the engine does\\\\n406:### 4.2 The substrate mapping\\\\n474:### 4.3 Primitive procedures\\\\n543:### 4.4 The transition table\\\\n553:#### 4.4.1 Copy, assignment and references\\\\n645:#### 4.4.2 Calls, arguments and temporaries\\\\n859:#### 4.4.3 Iteration\\\\n989:#### 4.4.4 Unset\\\\n1005:#### 4.4.5 Typed properties and references\\\\n1106:#### 4.4.6 Objects: finalization, clone and readonly\\\\n1208:#### 4.4.