st parses: **95 unique quick IDs, six slow records**, both passing records removed, and timeout/resource classes distinguished correctly. However, the inspected artifacts still lack measured-tree hashes and run references for the older `bug44069` and `bug40809` measurements. Your brief identifies the final-tip `bug63055` verification; my local repeat reached its review cutoff without a result.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**(b) CONFIRMED.** The no-buffer arms emit errno **8**, preserve the recorded messages, and return **false**. The fixture compares diagnostics directly, without suppression. A focused `ob_end_clean()` probe reproduced the exact notice and `false`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**(c) DEFECT.** B1-r2 removes the nested-encoding host error and repairs several counterexamples, but focused probes on this tip reproduce remaining defects:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **Array comparison:** default `array_unique([\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1.0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"])` retains one value; PHP requires two because its default is `SORT_STRING`. The test now pins the wrong default. [Implementation](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:526), [PHP source](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/php-8.3.35/ext/standard/array.c).\\\\\\\\n- **JSON failure/depth:** `json_encode([INF])` still emits an unwanted warning; `json_encode([[1]],0,1)` still succeeds. PHP returns `false` without that warning and rejects the depth overflow. [Failure path](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:673), [PHP failure handling](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/php-8.3.35/ext/json/json.c), [depth handling](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/php-8.3.35/ext/json/json_encoder.c).\\\\\\\\n- **JSON grammar:** removing `+` everywhere also rejects valid `1e+2`, returning `NULL`. [Scanner](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:808), [PHP grammar](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/php-8.3.35/ext/json/json_scanner.re).\\\\\\\\n- **Extract:** nonexistent `EXTR_PREFIX_ONLY_IF_EXISTS` remains defined as `7`, and mode `7` is accepted; PHP rejects it. [Constant](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/builtins.cljc:171), [PHP validation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/php-8.3.35/ext/standard/array.c).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe **3/158/0** gate therefore does not close the contract findings.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Landing authority: HOLD P8 at `06cd429f`; no unconditional landing authority.** Read-only review; no files changed.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\ncollab/orch-lane/1794990000000-architect-p8-final-confirm2.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:31:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_15\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc 'ls /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/.cpcache && cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/collab/orch-lane/1794950000000-engineer-p8-final-items.muse-spark-1.3-contributor.findings.md && git -C /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8 rev-parse HEAD'\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2072761871.basis\\\\\\\\n2072761871.cp\\\\\\\\n2072761871.main\\\\\\\\n2276128749.basis\\\\\\\\n2276128749.cp\\\\\\\\n2484545867.basis\\\\\\\\n2484545867.cp\\\\\\\\n3644903311.basis\\\\\\\\n3644903311.cp\\\\\\\\n3644903311.jvm\\\\\\\\n3644903311.main\\\\\\\\n3644903311.manifest\\\\\\\\n4183786633.basis\\\\\\\\n4183786633.cp\\\\\\\\n4183786633.jvm\\\\\\\\n4183786633.main\\\\\\\\n4183786633.manifest\\\\\\\\n868029096.basis\\\\\\\\n868029096.cp\\\\\\\\n868029096.main\\\\\\\\n# P8 final items — engineer findings (muse-spark-1.3-contributor)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nTask: `/tmp/muse-p8-fixes.md` (provenance + four P9 contract residuals).\\\\\\\\nBranch: `feat/p8-legacy-retirement`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNote: the landing-review log named in the task\\\\\\\\n(`collab/orch-lane/1794900000000-architect-p8-final-confirm...stdout.log`)\\\\\\\\nis not present in this checkout (no `*arch*` under `/tmp`, no such entry\\\\\\\\nunder `collab/orch-lane/`), and `~/ci` does not exist on this laptop.\\\\\\\\nAll architect citations below are taken from the task file itself, which\\\\\\\\nquotes them with file:line precision; the cited lines (prelude_p9.cljc:673\\\\\\\\n`php/json-encode-fail`, prelude_p9.cljc:808 `php/json-number-end`,\\\\\\\\nbuiltins.cljc:171 EXTR constants) match the tree exactly.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 1. Provenance (`:measured-at` per slow-gap record)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n`test/yang/php/antlr/phpt_quick_mismatch_manifest.edn`: all 6\\\\\\\\n`:slow-known-gaps` records now carry a one-line `:measured-at` map\\\\\\\\n`{:tree ... :host \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"shiva\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" :date ... :log ...}` (EDN-validated: 6 gaps,\\\\\\\\n6 measured):\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- `bug40809` → `{:tree \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"dbe9e072\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" :date \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2026-11-05\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n  :log \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"~/ci/rm-40809-long.log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}` (the 90-min remeasure).\\\\\\\\n- The other five (`gc_013`, `gc_023`, `bug39438`, `bug64660`, `gc_012`) →\\\\\\\\n  `{:tree \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"06cd429f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" :date \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2026-11-04\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" :log \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"~/ci/rm-phpt-quick.log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}`.\\\\\\\\n- `bug44069` / `bug63055` have no records to annotate: both were removed\\\\\\\\n  after they passed on the measured trees (`514fae8d`, `c65fb4b1`).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 2. P9 contract residuals\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(a) `array_unique` default is `SORT_STRING` (`prelude_p9.cljc`,\\\\\\\\n`php/bi-array-unique`): default flag `0` → `2`. The old test pinned the\\\\\\\\nloose-equality behavior (`array_unique(['1.0','1'])` → `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1.0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`); it now\\\\\\\\nexpects `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1.0,1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`, with explicit `SORT_STRING` / `SORT_NUMERIC` /\\\\\\\\n`SORT_REGULAR` pins alongside.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(b) `json_encode` failure path (`php/json-encode-fail`): non-throw mode\\\\\\\\nnow answers `false` with no warning (the `php/warn` call is removed);\\\\\\\\nthrow mode unchanged. Depth: a container now fails when\\\\\\\\n`(>= (+ depth 1) maxdepth)` — the top-level container is depth level 1,\\\\\\\\nso `json_encode([1], 0, 1)` fails, consistent with the decode side\\\\\\\\n(`json_decode('[1]', true, 1)` → NULL, already covered). Boundary note:\\\\\\\\nat the default depth 512 this allows 511 nesting levels rather than 512;\\\\\\\\nno test covers that extreme and no PHP binary exists on this laptop to\\\\\\\\narbitrate it — flagged, not verified.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(c) JSON scanner (`php/json-number-end` + `php/json-number`): the scan\\\\\\\\nnow admits `+` (43) so `1e+2` / `1E+2` are single tokens; validation\\\\\\\\nrequires a whole number (`php/full-num?`, which also rejects truncated\\\\\\\\nforms like `1e`, `1e+`, `1+` that the old `:php/null` check accepted as\\\\\\\\n`:leading` prefixes) and rejects leading-`+` / leading-zero tokens via\\\\\\\\nthe new `php/json-lead-bad?` (`+1`, `01`, `-01` → NULL).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(d) `EXTR_PREFIX_ONLY_IF_EXISTS` (`builtins.cljc:171`): constant removed\\\\\\\\nfrom `builtins/constants` (so `defined()` is false and a bare read is the\\\\\\\\nstandard lowering refusal, not a fold); `php/bi-extract` refuses mode 7\\\\\\\\nwith `ValueError` (`> flags 6`); the dead mode-7 branches in\\\\\\\\n`php/extract-needs-prefix?` / `php/extract-target` are removed.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Gate\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Focused regressions were added first and observed failing (8 failures,\\\\\\\\n  each the architect's counterexample), then fixed: `builtin-surfaces-test`\\\\\\\\n  167 assertions, 0 failures.\\\\\\\\n- `clojure -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.builtin-surfaces-test -n yang.php.antlr.request-context-test` → 6 tests, 202 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors.\\\\\\\\n- `clojure -M:kondo --lint` on th