e, so the\\\\npair is impossible. The engine-results were recorded from the Nov-4 oracle\\\\npass (manifest regenerated in `2e5f7f2f`, 2026-11-04 12:36 +0700); the exact\\\\nshiva checkout hash of that run was never recorded, so per the task brief no\\\\nhash was invented: all five now carry `:tree \\\\\\\"unrecorded\\\\\\\"`, keeping the\\\\nsupported `:date \\\\\\\"2026-11-04\\\\\\\"`, `:host \\\\\\\"shiva\\\\\\\"`, and `:log\\\\n\\\\\\\"~/ci/rm-phpt-quick.log\\\\\\\"`. `bug40809` keeps `{:tree \\\\\\\"dbe9e072\\\\\\\" :date\\\\n\\\\\\\"2026-11-05\\\\\\\" :log \\\\\\\"~/ci/rm-40809-long.log\\\\\\\"}` (the 90-min remeasure; already\\\\ncorrect). No code reads `:measured-at` (EDN data only); re-validated 6 gaps,\\\\n6 measured via `clojure.edn`.\\\\n\\\\n## 2. JSON depth off-by-one (`prelude_p9.cljc`, `php/json-encode`)\\\\n\\\\nThe container guard was `(>= (+ depth 1) maxdepth)`, failing `[1]` at depth\\\\n1. Now `(> (+ depth 1) maxdepth)`: `json_encode([1],0,1)` → `\\\\\\\"[1]\\\\\\\"`,\\\\n`json_encode([[1]],0,1)` → `false`. Test pins updated in\\\\n`builtin_surfaces_test.clj`: the `[1],0,1` var_dump pin is now `string(3)\\\\n\\\\\\\"[1]\\\\\\\"` (diag still `[]`), plus a new `[[1]],0,1` → `bool(false)` pin. The\\\\nnew pins failed before the fix (3 failures incl. the two scanner pins) and\\\\npass after.\\\\n\\\\n## 3. JSON number scanner (`prelude_p9.cljc`, `php/json-number`)\\\\n\\\\n`php/num-prefix` (PHP juggling; untouched) accepts `.1` and `1.` as full\\\\nnumbers, but the JSON grammar needs digits on both sides of the point. Added\\\\n`php/json-dot-bad-at` / `php/json-dot-bad?`: any `.` in the token without a\\\\ndigit on both sides is a syntax error. `1e+2` stays valid (no point in the\\\\ntoken); `1e+` truncation and leading-plus/leading-zero rejection unchanged.\\\\nNew pins: `json_decode('.1')` and `json_decode('1.')` → `NULL`.\\\\n\\\\n## Gate\\\\n\\\\n- `clojure -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.builtin-surfaces-test -n\\\\n  yang.php.antlr.request-context-t