{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"agent_message","text":"**Step-7: DEFECT at `520f8a3f`.** Read-only review and focused JVM probes completed; no files changed.\n\n1. **CONFIRMED — three escalation rulings.** Request binding runs inside the root handler after terminal escapes are installed: [prelude.cljc:5462](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5462). An injected initialization Throwable produced the expected snapshot with empty output and no body execution. Invalid levels throw `ValueError` with the pinned message: [prelude.cljc:779](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:779). Both profiles accept requests; linked runtime cells remain task-local: [lower.cljc:3790](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3790), [prelude.cljc:5804](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5804).\n\n2. **CONFIRMED — integer-key merge.** Keys are preserved, colliding scalars overwritten, and colliding arrays recursively merged: [prelude.cljc:425](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:425). Sparse and nested integer collisions have fixtures.\n\n3. **DEFECT — guest-fatal cleanup remains incomplete.** Matching handlers returning non-false correctly continue, and guest-fatal preserves shutdown functions and buffers. However, it never marks existing objects destructed before ordinary shutdown: [prelude.cljc:742](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:742), [prelude.cljc:4217](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:4217). A probe produced `BSD`—buffer, shutdown, **destructor**—where the destructor should be suppressed. Fatal status `255` is also absent. [PHP 8.3 fatal handling](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/main/main.c) establishes both requirements.\n\n4. **DEFECT — stream P2 remains open.** The harness consumes the request before lowering; lowering still embeds it in UAST: [lower.cljc:3791](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3791). Response and diagnostic vectors are copied into streams **after VM completion**: [portable_harness.cljc:214](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/test/yang/php/antlr/portable_harness.cljc:214). Runtime emission still appends to cells. Header replacement additionally deletes earlier response records: [prelude.cljc:580](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:580); replacement should be interpreted from appended commands.\n\n5. **DEFECT — HTTP/cookie/oracle residuals.**\n   - Status-line parsing and the two-handler/mask fixture are implemented.\n   - `http_response_code(0)` still checks headers-sent before recognizing the getter: [prelude.cljc:613](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:613). After output, the probe returned false plus a warning.\n   - Cookie excess arguments throw `ValueError` instead of `ArgumentCountError`; unknown-option messages differ, and array-option coercions were removed: [prelude.cljc:647](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:647), [prelude.cljc:670](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:670). These disagree with [PHP 8.3’s implementation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/standard/head.c).\n   - B2 enumeration, nested serialization, recursive merge, and HTTP scaffolding are present. But plain fatal parsing populates both `:uncaught` and `:fatal`, leaving the expected fatal diagnostic absent: [oracle.clj:139](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj:139). Fold output drops `:fatal` and exit status: [oracle.clj:471](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj:471). Pending fixtures are excluded from failures, so a zero exit is not acceptance evidence.\n\n6. **CONFIRMED — reported focused gate: 7/153